## Nothing compounds automatically

Workers do not read any memory store: every worker starts cold, from its
issue and the repo alone. (The `memory/shared/` layers a session may have
mounted are context for the **coordinator** session — they are not something a
dispatched worker reads back.) So a finding that should shape *future* work
has to be put somewhere load-bearing by hand: the repo's `CLAUDE.md` for a
repo convention, a skill for a general working practice, a follow-up issue for
a concrete fix, or your own `memory/` notes for coordinator context. Filing an
investigation is not the same as the project having learned from it.

At the end of a session, update your memory index with anything worth
carrying forward — one fact per file, one line per fact in the index. When the
operator gives explicit direction ("remember that…"), write it immediately
rather than waiting for the end of the session.
